records.message:
docs(release): add version/release mechanism design rationale

Record the design intent behind the version/release pipeline so it is not mistaken
for replaceable scaffolding:
- machine-fits-human: version intent is read from the branch-channel flow developers
  already perform, requiring zero per-change declaration;
- the git tag is the artifact; package.json version is a downstream projection;
- a release tag = code-freeze (X) binary-distribution, performed atomically (kungfu
  ships prebuilt cross-platform binaries, unlike source-distributed ecosystems);
- release-worthiness is enforced by an un-cheatable pipeline (3-platform verify +
  review + strict checks, isAdminEnforced), not by judgment;
- weak-centralization: a release is the promotion of a user-validated alpha, not any
  one developer's unilateral call.

Explains why changesets/semantic-release are a downgrade in this context and lists
replacement criteria, so future maintainers (human or AI) don't swap it out blindly.
